<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's short-term memory register (the body's bot.register): a bounded
  rolling record of the stimuli the body admitted and of the turns, in
  words, the bot heard and said. It is sensory short-term memory at the
  event layer, not a durable memory stream. The body (bots/floppy/floppy.scx)
  invokes it as its child "stm" and reaches it by message only.

    opening -> serving { idle -request-> applying.<operation> -> idle }
    opening -no memory-> absent
    opening -open failed or timed out-> degraded

  Input: the <param>s memory (the address of the bot's memory, decision
  D262; none: absent), and its bounds:
  capacity (64 stimuli), recency_window_ms (5 min), turn_capacity (32
  turns), turn_window_ms (10 min), open_timeout_ms (30 s).

  opening asks the bot's memory (abilities/memory/memory.scx, decision
  D262, which migrated the database to floppy's head revision, 0001,
  which holds bot_stm_memory and bot_stm_turn) for one read of
  bot_stm_turn, then
  sends bot.ability.ready to the parent once (decision D242): the
  register offers nothing to the cognition. A database that cannot be opened (logged as
  stm.open.failed, "short-term memory could not open its database: ...")
  or does not open within open_timeout_ms leaves it degraded, never ready, so the body's activation fails at its timeout; on entering
  degraded it sends bot.ability.failed {message: "unavailable: short-term
  memory is degraded."} to the parent.
  Without a memory it logs <log label="memory" expr="'absent'">, is ready,
  and holds nothing: notifications are dropped and reads answer empty.

  Notifications (no reply; the sender never waits on perception upkeep):
  - bot.ability.memory.stm.record {stimulus_name, payload, event_id?,
    source?, target?} (which the producer builds with
    <memory:stm_projection>; its schema holds the payload to non-empty keys
    and strings of at most 40 characters) inserts one row into bot_stm_memory
    (payload_json the projection with sorted keys and compact separators,
    created_at now) and, in the same transaction, evicts every row beyond
    capacity by the effective clock COALESCE(last_accessed_at, created_at),
    newest kept.
  - bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce {stm_ids} stamps last_accessed_at
    now on those rows, so used signals outlive arrival churn.
  - bot.ability.memory.stm.turn {id, direction, speakers, text, cut,
    conversation} inserts one row into
    bot_stm_turn (at now) and, in the same transaction, when the table is
    over turn_capacity, sheds the older half at once (the newest
    turn_capacity - floor(turn_capacity / 2) stay), so the oldest turn a
    read returns stays put between sheds. The producer cuts the words with
    <memory:cut_at_word>; the register cuts them again (a no-op on cut
    words) because no schema can bound UTF-8 bytes, and cut is true when
    either cut them. Words that cut to nothing (only white space before
    the bound) are not
    written, and are logged as stm.failed.
  A notification that fails is logged as stm.failed ("short-term memory
  <event> failed: ..."); nobody is told.

  Requests (each answered to the parent, in arrival order):
  - bot.ability.memory.stm.recent {stimulus_name?, limit?} reads the rows
    whose effective clock is inside recency_window_ms, optionally for one
    stimulus, newest first, at most limit (default recent_limit, 64), and
    answers bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.output {entries} (each stm_id,
    stimulus_name, payload, event_id, source, target, created_at,
    last_accessed_at).
  - bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns {limit?, within?} reads the
    newest turns, at most limit (default recent_turns_limit, 32), written
    at or after the floor, and answers
    bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output {turns} oldest first (each
    id, at, direction, speakers, text, cut, conversation; a stored row that
    does not decode as one is skipped). The window is turn_window_ms, or
    within (milliseconds) when that is shorter; the floor is now less the
    window, moved down to a whole step of half the window since the Unix epoch, so
    a turn is read for at least the window and at most one and a half.
  A request that fails is answered bot.ability.failed {message: "short-term
  memory <event> failed: ..."}. SCXML stamps no reply with its request's
  id, so a requester tells answers apart by order: the register applies
  one operation at a time.

  Times are ISO 8601 UTC text, so text order is time order, and a turn's
  at is answered as stored. A row id is the next of the 32-digit
  zero-padded ids (neither engine's randomness is unique across
  invocations in Wasm), so id order is insertion order. The SQL runs on
  both engines (SQLite and Postgres).

  Deferral: every request and notification that
  arrives while opening or applying is held by <event:defer/> (scxml.rs
  namespaces/event) and taken, in order, once the register is idle.

  degraded: requests are answered bot.ability.failed {message:
  "unavailable: short-term memory is degraded."}; notifications are dropped and
  logged as stm.dropped.

  Logs: memory ('absent'), stm.open.failed, stm.turn.recorded ("<direction>
  cut=<true|false>"), stm.failed, stm.dropped.

  Contracts: every event it takes names its abilities/schemas/ file by
  event:schema. A send or raise whose data does not satisfy it is
  error.execution in its sender, and input from outside the session that
  does not is refused, so no cond rechecks a payload.

  Bindings: the memory namespace package (the bot's memory, which the
  body invokes, binds the sql and pgsql service packages).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       xmlns:memory="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/memory"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="stm" initial="opening">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The invoker's <param>s: the memory's address (null: absent) and the
         bounds. -->
    <data id="memory" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The id of each request this document last sent the memory, by
         the state that sent it (decision D262). -->
    <data id="memory_requests" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="capacity" expr="64"/>
    <data id="recency_window_ms" expr="300000"/>
    <data id="turn_capacity" expr="32"/>
    <data id="turn_window_ms" expr="600000"/>
    <data id="open_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <!-- The reads' default limits (fixed whatever the capacities are). -->
    <data id="recent_limit" expr="64"/>
    <data id="recent_turns_limit" expr="32"/>
    <!-- The operation in hand: its event's data, and a turn's words as
         <memory:cut_at_word> bounds them. -->
    <data id="request" expr="null"/>
    <data id="bounded" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The statements (written for both engines). -->
    <data id="open_select" expr="'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bot_stm_turn'"/>
    <data id="record_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_stm_memory (stm_id, stimulus_name, payload_json, event_id, source, target, created_at) VALUES ((SELECT substr(\'00000000000000000000000000000000\', 1, 32 - length(n)) || n FROM (SELECT CAST(COALESCE(MAX(CAST(stm_id AS BIGINT)), 0) + 1 AS TEXT) AS n FROM bot_stm_memory) AS c), ?1, ?2, ?3, ?4, ?5, ?6)'"/>
    <data id="record_evict" expr="'DELETE FROM bot_stm_memory WHERE stm_id NOT IN (SELECT stm_id FROM bot_stm_memory ORDER BY COALESCE(last_accessed_at, created_at) DESC, stm_id DESC LIMIT ?1)'"/>
    <data id="reinforce_update" expr="'UPDATE bot_stm_memory SET last_accessed_at = ?1 WHERE stm_id IN'"/>
    <data id="recent_select" expr="'SELECT stm_id, stimulus_name, payload_json, event_id, source, target, created_at, last_accessed_at FROM bot_stm_memory WHERE COALESCE(last_accessed_at, created_at) >= ?1 ORDER BY COALESCE(last_accessed_at, created_at) DESC, stm_id DESC LIMIT ?2'"/>
    <data id="recent_named_select" expr="'SELECT stm_id, stimulus_name, payload_json, event_id, source, target, created_at, last_accessed_at FROM bot_stm_memory WHERE COALESCE(last_accessed_at, created_at) >= ?1 AND stimulus_name = ?2 ORDER BY COALESCE(last_accessed_at, created_at) DESC, stm_id DESC LIMIT ?3'"/>
    <data id="turn_insert" expr="'INSERT INTO bot_stm_turn (turn_id, at, direction, speakers_json, text, cut, conversation) VALUES (?1, ?2, ?3, ?4, ?5, ?6, ?7)'"/>
    <data id="turn_shed" expr="'DELETE FROM bot_stm_turn WHERE (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM bot_stm_turn) > ?1 AND seq NOT IN (SELECT seq FROM bot_stm_turn ORDER BY seq DESC LIMIT ?2)'"/>
    <data id="recent_turns_select" expr="'SELECT turn_id, at, direction, speakers_json, text, cut, conversation FROM bot_stm_turn WHERE at >= ?1 ORDER BY seq DESC LIMIT ?2'"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="stm.js"/>

  <!-- Open the register's tables in the memory before
       serving anything; what arrives meanwhile waits. -->
  <state id="opening" initial="opening_from">
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.record" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.record.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.turn.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.json">
      <event:defer/>
    </transition>
    <state id="opening_from">
      <transition cond="hasNoMemory()" target="absent"/>
      <transition target="opening_memory"/>
    </state>
    <state id="opening_memory">
      <onentry>
        <send id="opening-after" event="opening.after" delayexpr="delay(open_timeout_ms)"/>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="opening-after"/>
      </onexit>
      <onentry>
        <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.open">
          <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.open"/>
          <param name="statements" expr="openStatements()"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('open')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="serving">
        <send event="bot.ability.ready" target="#_parent"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('open')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="degraded">
        <log label="stm.open.failed" expr="openFailedMessage(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="degraded">
        <log label="stm.open.failed" expr="openFailedMessage(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="opening.after" target="degraded">
        <log label="stm.open.failed" expr="'short-term memory could not open its database: it did not open in time.'"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- One operation at a time over the bot's memory. -->
  <state id="serving" initial="idle">
    <state id="idle">
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.record" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.record.json" target="recording">
        <assign location="request" expr="_event.data"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce.json" target="reinforcing">
        <assign location="request" expr="_event.data"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.turn.json" target="bounding_turn">
        <assign location="request" expr="_event.data"/>
        <memory:cut_at_word location="bounded" words="_event.data.text"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.json" target="reading">
        <assign location="request" expr="_event.data"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.json" target="reading_turns">
        <assign location="request" expr="_event.data"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- Requests are applied one at a time; the rest wait. -->
    <state id="applying" initial="recording">
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.record" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.record.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.turn.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>

      <!-- Record one stimulus projection, evicting beyond capacity in the
           same transaction. -->
      <state id="recording">
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.record">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.record"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="recordStatements()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('record')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="idle"/>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('record')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.failed" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.record', _event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.failed" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.record', _event)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Stamp the access time on the entries grounding relied on. -->
      <state id="reinforcing">
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.reinforce">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.reinforce"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="reinforceStatements()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('reinforce')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="idle"/>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('reinforce')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.failed" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce', _event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.failed" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce', _event)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Record one turn, shedding the older half beyond turn_capacity in
           the same transaction. -->
      <!-- Words that cut to nothing (white space up to the bound) are no
           turn: a stored empty text would fail every later read. -->
      <state id="bounding_turn">
        <transition cond="isEmptyTurn()" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.failed" expr="emptyTurnMessage()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition target="recording_turn"/>
      </state>

      <state id="recording_turn">
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.turn">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.turn"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="turnStatements()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('turn')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.turn.recorded" expr="turnRecordedLog()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('turn')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.failed" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.turn', _event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="idle">
          <log label="stm.failed" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.turn', _event)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Read the stimuli inside the recency window, newest first. -->
      <state id="reading">
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.recent">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.recent"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="recentStatements()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('recent')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.output" target="#_parent">
            <param name="entries" expr="recentEntries(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('recent')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.recent', _event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.recent', _event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Read the newest turns since the floor, answered oldest first. -->
      <state id="reading_turns">
        <onentry>
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.input" targetexpr="memory" idlocation="memory_requests.recent_turns">
            <param name="id" expr="memory_requests.recent_turns"/>
            <param name="statements" expr="recentTurnsStatements()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <transition event="bot.ability.memory.output" cond="isMemoryReply('recent_turns')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.output.json" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output" target="#_parent">
            <param name="turns" expr="recentTurns(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="isMemoryReply('recent_turns')" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns', _event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
            <param name="message" expr="operationFailedMessage('bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns', _event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- No memory: ready, and holding nothing. -->
  <state id="absent">
    <onentry>
      <log label="memory" expr="'absent'"/>
      <send event="bot.ability.ready" target="#_parent"/>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.record" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.record.json"/>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce.json"/>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.turn.json"/>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.output" target="#_parent">
        <param name="entries" expr="[]"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.output" target="#_parent">
        <param name="turns" expr="[]"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- The database could not be opened: nothing is served, and the
       parent is told why. -->
  <state id="degraded">
    <onentry>
      <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
        <param name="message" expr="'unavailable: short-term memory is degraded.'"/>
      </send>
    </onentry>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.record" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.record.json">
      <log label="stm.dropped" expr="'degraded'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.reinforce.json">
      <log label="stm.dropped" expr="'degraded'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.turn" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.turn.json">
      <log label="stm.dropped" expr="'degraded'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
        <param name="message" expr="'unavailable: short-term memory is degraded.'"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.memory.stm.recent_turns.json">
      <send event="bot.ability.failed" target="#_parent">
        <param name="message" expr="'unavailable: short-term memory is degraded.'"/>
      </send>
    </transition>
  </state>
</scxml>
